  "final": "I added `clamp(value, lower, upper)` to `src/numbers.py`, and `python3 checks/public.py` passes.\n\n- **Behavior:** it returns `lower` when `value` is below the range and `upper` when it's above. Otherwise it returns `value` unchanged, so both bounds are inclusive. If `lower > upper`, it raises `ValueError`. That check runs before any comparison with `value`.\n- **`add`:** unchanged.\n- **Checks:** I added cases to `checks/public.py` for:\n  - a value inside the range;\n  - a value below and a value above;\n  - a value equal to each bound;\n  - `lower == upper`;\n  - a float value;\n  - the `ValueError` case.\n\n  The original `add` assertion is still there.\n\nI only changed files in `src/` and `checks/`.",
